Subject: [PATCH] coff64-rs6000: allow 16-bit signed TLS LE relocs

Go's AIX/ppc64 external linker rewrites the local-exec TLS addis/addi
sequence into a single addi against R13 and emits an XCOFF R_TLS_LE
relocation with r_size 0x0f for the 16-bit immediate field.  The XCOFF64
relocation pass already has machinery to honor the r_size-encoded width
for relocation types whose field size can vary, but only R_POS and R_NEG
use it.

Allow R_TLS_LE to use the same size adjustment so 16-bit TLS LE relocations
can be applied to the rewritten instruction field instead of being rejected
as a wrong r_rsize.  The rewritten addi uses a signed 16-bit displacement,
so treat the 16-bit TLS LE form as signed for overflow checking even when
the input r_size omits the signed bit.

--- a/bfd/coff64-rs6000.c	2026-06-30 16:31:09.869071740 +0000
+++ b/bfd/coff64-rs6000.c	2026-07-14 17:46:17.914060630 +0000
@@ -1586,6 +1586,7 @@
 	    {
 	    case R_POS:
 	    case R_NEG:
+	    case R_TLS_LE:
 	      howto.bitsize = (rel->r_size & 0x3f) + 1;
 	      howto.size = HOWTO_RSIZE (howto.bitsize <= 16
 					? 2 : howto.bitsize <= 32
@@ -1605,6 +1606,8 @@
       howto.complain_on_overflow = (rel->r_size & 0x80
 				    ? complain_overflow_signed
 				    : complain_overflow_bitfield);
+      if (rel->r_type == R_TLS_LE && howto.bitsize == 16)
+	howto.complain_on_overflow = complain_overflow_signed;
 
       /* symbol */
       val = 0;
